<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip IV of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a>–<a href="/years/1665">1665</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> was king of Spain and Portugal from 1621 to 1665. With his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares">Olivares</a> he fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and the renewed war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, and the heavy demands of war provoked the revolts of Catalonia and Portugal in 1640. Portugal regained its independence, and Spain's power declined, though his court was painted by Velázquez.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-spain.jpg" alt="Philip IV of Spain" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Velázquez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_IV_of_Spain_-_Vel%C3%A1zquez_1644.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
